comments[17]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-17T01:29:50.524Z",codex-agent,"Round 3: read the full unresolved PR 1 text-performance thread at ef95044. Plan: bound every input field to 512 code points at complete grapheme boundaries before XML validation, measurement and metadata; use cumulative glyph advances for linear ellipsizing; add deterministic measurement budgets, grapheme and boundary coverage plus a behavioral revert proof."
  "2026-10-17T01:32:51.225Z",codex-agent,"Implemented a bounded 513-code-point lookahead window and complete-grapheme cap of 512 before validation, layout and metadata. Ellipsizing measures each bounded glyph once and scans cumulative advances at grapheme boundaries. Revert proof: old ellipsize exceeds the 513-call budget both without and with the new cap; removing the cap fails exact/one-over boundaries. All 4 round-three behavioral mutations were caught and restored, including the tag mismatch check."
  "2026-10-17T01:36:20.672Z",codex-agent,"Final verification: npm run release:check passed with isolated HOME and clean Git configuration; bun run release:check passed sequentially. Each gate: 25/25 tests, zero skips/cancellations/todos, all src coverage 100/100/100/100, packed npm and Bun consumers passed. Focused pm test run passed 9/9. Revert proof passed 4/4 mutations; old algorithm fails at glyph measurement call 514 with or without the cap. Existing image snapshots pass unchanged. No remaining implementation risks found within the bounded rendering path."
  "2026-10-17T09:37:56.851Z",codex-agent,"Phase bhxl: reuse this generator feature for the committed public fleet banner set. Inventory: all 26 public fleet package repositories except pm-cli, including this kit; exact package names and one-line package.json descriptions are captured in banners/packages.json. Generate fixed light/dark SVG pairs with path lettering and fail on stale, missing or surplus output. Compare SVG and PNG on both GitHub theme grounds before choosing the immutable README embed format. Identity fix PR #4 is pushed; no release is authorized."
  "2026-10-17T09:55:46.025Z",codex-agent,"Validation: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 50/50 tests, zero failures or skips, and 100/100/100/100 source coverage. Both packed npm/Bun consumers pass; the allow-listed pack contains 130 intended files. Behavioral revert: removing only the stale-content comparison in generateBanners makes the unchanged stale-gate test fail 1/1; restoring it passes the 3/3 package-banner suite. SVG and PNG were reviewed at 1x/2x in light/dark at all three widths; SVG retains crisp outlines. All 52 images decode with no horizontal page overflow. Review PNGs: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brand/tree/pr-screenshots/brand/package-banners . The release stays held."
  "2026-10-17T12:18:04.102Z",codex-agent,"Round 1: strip npm scope only for banner display, preserve exact catalog package names, regenerate both pm-web themes and verify the stale asset gate. Compare every catalog description against its repository README without editing other packages."
  "2026-10-17T12:18:10.634Z",codex-agent,"Round 1: strip npm scope only for banner display, preserve exact catalog names, regenerate both pm-web themes and verify the stale-file gate. Compare every catalog description against its repository README without editing other packages."
  "2026-10-17T12:22:39.606Z",codex-agent,"Description audit: all 26 catalog entries exactly match their package.json descriptions. Follow-up pm-brand-description-followup records four weak or stale summaries: pm-github, pm-rl, pm-web and pm-gantt-chart. Other repositories remain unedited. Scope regression: regenerating with only the display-scope fix reverted fails the unchanged scoped-name test; restoring it regenerates 52 banners and passes 4/4 tests."
  "2026-10-17T12:26:17.022Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 validation: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 51/51 tests, zero failures/skips, 100/100/100/100 source coverage, 52 deterministic assets, and packed npm/Bun consumers. The scope behavioral revert fails its 1/1 unchanged regression. Current banner linked test passes 4/4; three inherited linked commands were refused for foreign branch provenance and were not used as evidence. Twelve 2x review captures decode, have no horizontal overflow or external requests, and were published under brand/package-banners/round1 on pr-screenshots. Release remains held."
  "2026-10-17T12:32:59.971Z",codex-agent,"Stack correction: carried identity PR 4 commit 3e7af696902f37ca0734a524897764d881ef817c onto this branch so it cannot retain the old bootstrap fallback. The earlier 51/51 full-gate results apply to the scope-only commit; both current release gates now fail closed until trusted controls are independently adopted on main. Verify the combined 58-test suite and downstream package checks before final delivery."
  "2026-10-17T12:36:02.525Z",codex-agent,"Combined head validation after carrying the hardened identity gate: 58/58 tests pass, zero failures/skips, 100/100/100/100 source coverage; tracker health, typecheck, lint, build parity, docstrings, assets/fonts, 52 deterministic banners, production audit, 130 intended packed files and packed npm/Bun consumers pass separately. npm run release:check and bun run release:check both fail closed on missing trusted main controls. Scope code/tests/assets are byte-identical to the earlier reviewed correction and its 12 captures. Independent control adoption is the remaining blocker; no release is authorized."
  "2026-10-18T03:02:50.543Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 CI diagnosis: both Node checks fail only because PR 5 is stacked on PR 4 and trusted main controls are absent. Keep the bare pm-name display. PR 152 updates the Gantt package description to include ASCII, SVG, HTML, Mermaid, dependency-aware scheduling and Triplicate styling; banners refresh when the generator next re-reads package descriptions. Bootstrap currently also exposes an older main identity-gate failure on inherited squash history."
  "2026-10-18T05:08:29.207Z",codex-agent,"Round 3: refresh banners against independently adopted main controls after the identity branch is pushed. Retain the trusted-base implementation when main conflicts with the seed gate, verify both release gates, and leave release held and PR unmerged."
  "2026-10-18T05:14:15.780Z",codex-agent,Main refresh retains the exact trusted-base identity implementation from PR 4 and replaces the older root anchor with the independently adopted forward baseline from PR 6. Identity check now succeeds against main 98cbe45976b3111f09143c2a29ede906cb553c2a. Banner code and all 52 reviewed images are unchanged; the four banner regressions are run through their existing linked command. Full isolated npm/Bun release gates are running and exact-head CI will confirm both Node versions. Release remains held.
  "2026-10-18T08:40:32.892Z",codex-agent,"Review round 5 PR5: reject generated light/dark filename collisions with regression and revert proof. Workflow and ancestry findings belong to PR4; integrate the updated PR4 branch rather than diverging. Release remains HELD."
  "2026-10-18T08:43:51.596Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: node scripts/banner-revert-proof.ts removes only the collision guard in a disposable copy and the unchanged regression fails with Missing expected exception. node --test test/package-banners.test.ts passes 5/5, including both catalog orders and both generation modes with no output writes on rejection."
  "2026-10-18T08:49:29.571Z",codex-agent,"Integrated PR4 head 06454bdcb9cd26d70ed1c0419218e89ed7bea3dd, taking its identity code and workflow definitions verbatim. Both CI review findings and the trusted-baseline ancestry regression are owned there. Retained banner documentation, inspected the sole cache receipt with its tracked twin and operation, then reconciled it with the pinned CLI without rewriting history. Trusted workflow activation remains blocked on independent main adoption and administrator-required enforcement."
